-- title:
--   Closed subscheme cut out by a base-change-compatible family of ideals
-- statement:
--   Let $E$ be a scheme (in a fixed universe $u$). Suppose given a rule $I$ which assigns, to every commutative ring $R$ whose carrier lies in $u$ and every morphism $s : \operatorname{Spec} R \to E$, an ideal $I(R,s) \subseteq R$; no continuity or coherence is assumed beyond the single compatibility hypothesis $hI$, namely that for all rings $R, R'$, every ring homomorphism $\psi : R \to R'$ and every $s : \operatorname{Spec} R \to E$, the ideal attached to the composite $\operatorname{Spec} \psi$ followed by $s$ is the ideal of $R'$ generated by $\psi(I(R,s))$, i.e. $I(R', \operatorname{Spec}\psi \,\text{followed by}\, s) = \psi_*I(R,s)$ in the sense of `Ideal.map`. The conclusion asserts the existence of a scheme $Z$ and a morphism $\iota : Z \to E$ which is a closed immersion, such that for every commutative ring $R$ in the universe and every morphism $s : \operatorname{Spec} R \to E$ the following are equivalent: there is a morphism $z : \operatorname{Spec} R \to Z$ with $z$ followed by $\iota$ equal to $s$; and $I(R,s) = 0$. Only affine test objects occur in the stated equivalence, and only existence (not uniqueness) of the factorisation $z$ is asserted.
--
--   This is the representability of a closed subfunctor of the functor of points of $E$ defined by the vanishing of a base-change-compatible family of ideals on affine points: such a family is the data of a quasi-coherent ideal sheaf on $E$, and $Z$ is the corresponding closed subscheme. It is used in the project as the general mechanism for producing closed subschemes from pointwise ideal-theoretic conditions, being cited by [`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.exists_isOpenImmersion_isClosedImmersion_forall_exists_comp_eq_iff_of_ideal_of_isOpen`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.exists_isOpenImmersion_isClosedImmersion_forall_exists_comp_eq_iff_of_ideal_of_isOpen) and by [`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_isClosedImmersion_forall_factors_iff_of_idealCut`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.exists_isClosedImmersion_forall_factors_iff_of_idealCut).
